2,"d":2494,"h":"Mo-Fr 09:00-18:00; Sa 10:00-16:00; Su 11:00-16:00"},{"n":"Ica Wisborg","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":57.61745,"lo":18.284185,"d":2507,"h":"Mo-Su 06:00-21:00"},{"n":"Coop Gråbo","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":57.619114,"lo":18.301478,"d":2521,"w":"https://www.coop.se/butiker-erbjudanden/coop/coop-grabo/","ph":"+46 10 747 30 80"},{"n":"Almedalen","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":57.640556,"lo":18.290833,"d":352,"ds":"Almedalen (Swedish pronunciation: [ˈalmɛˈdɑːlɛn], lit. 'The Elm Valley') is a park in the Swedish city of Visby on the island of Gotland. It is well known in Sweden as the central site of the annual Almedalen Week. In medieval times the area, just outside the city walls was the city harbour.","wpu":"Almedalen","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b3/Mr_Bullitt_-_Almedalen_i_Visby.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Visborg","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":57.63543,"lo":18.28611,"d":512,"ds":"Visborg (also spelled Wisborg) was a medieval fortress located in the town of Visby on the Swedish island of Gotland. Several fortresses were built in Visby over the centuries. The last was the castle built by King Erik of Pomerania, ruler of Kalmar Union.","wpu":"Visborg","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Wisborg_Castle.jpg/960px-Wisborg_Castle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Vårdklockan Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":57.638333,"lo":18.295556,"d":655,"ds":"Vårdklockan Church is a church in Visby, on the island of Gotland in Sweden. It belongs to the Protestant Uniting Church in Sweden.","wpu":"Vårdklockan Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/V%C3%A5rdklockans_kyrka_Visby_Gotland_2.jpg/960px-V%C3%A5rdklockans_kyrka_Visby_Gotland_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Solberga Abbey","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":57.633528,"lo":18.29875,"d":1089,"ds":"Solberga Abbey (Swedish: Solberga kloster), was a Cistercian nunnery in Sweden, in operation from 1246 until at least 1469. It was located outside Visby on Gotland until 1404, and then in Visby. It was the only nunnery on the island of Gotland.","wpu":"Solberga Abbey","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Solberga_kloster.JPG/960px-Solberga_kloster.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Visborg Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":57.624444,"lo":18.285,"d":1729,"ds":"Visborg Church is a church in Visby, on the island of Gotland in Sweden. The church was built in 1969 and designed by architect Per Erik Nilsson. It's built of brick and pine wood.","wpu":"Visborg Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Visborgskyrkan..jpg/960px-Visborgskyrkan..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Vibble","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":57.6,"lo":18.25,"d":4911,"ds":"Vibble is a locality in Västerhejde on the Swedish island of Gotland. Sweden with 1,300 inhabitants in 2010. Situated 3 km (1.9 mi) south of Visby, it is sometimes regarded as a suburb to the town of Visby.","wpu":"Vibble","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Vibblecentrum.jpg/960px-Vibblecentrum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Stora Hästnäs","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":57.660167,"lo":18.3635,"d":5181,"ds":"Stora Hästnäs is an estate on the island Gotland, not far from Visby, Sweden. It is known mainly for its well preserved medieval era stone house dating from the 1300s. It is the most well-preserved medieval residential building on Gotland outside Visby.","wpu":"Stora Hästnäs","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/14th_century_stone_house%2C_Stora_H%C3%A4stn%C3%A4s%2C_Visby%2C_Gotland%2C_Sweden_%2825967633374%29.jpg/960px-14th_century_stone_house%2C_Stora_H%C3%A4stn%C3%A4s%2C_Visby%2C_Gotland%2C_Sweden_%2825967633374%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Västerhejde","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":57.583333,"lo":18.25,"d":6636,"ds":"Västerhejde is a locality on the Swedish island of Gotland. Västerhejde is also the name of the larger populated area known as a socken (not to be confused with parish). It comprises the same area as the administrative Västerhejde District, established on 1 January 2016.","wpu":"Västerhejde","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/25/H%C3%B6gklint_-_KMB_-_16001000012951.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Follingbo Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":57.5823,"lo":18.3833,"d":8685,"ds":"Follingbo Church (Swedish: Follingbo kyrka) is a medieval church in Follingbo on the Swedish island of Gotland. Its Romanesque nave and tower are noteworthy for the professionalism with which they were built. It lies in the Diocese of Visby and is used of the Church of Sweden.","wpu":"Follingbo Church","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0c/Follingbo-kyrka-T.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Träkumla Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":57.5603,"lo":18.313,"d":9017,"ds":"Träkumla Church (Swedish: Träkumla kyrka) is a medieval church on the Swedish island of Gotland, in the Baltic Sea. The church retains some murals and furnishings from the Middle Ages. It belongs to the Diocese of Visby.","wpu":"Träkumla Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Trakumla_kyrka_Gotland_Sverige_1.jpg/960px-Trakumla_kyrka_Gotland_Sverige_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Väskinde","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":57.683333,"lo":18.416667,"d":9195,"ds":"Väskinde (Swedish pronunciation: [ˈvɛ̂ɧːɪndɛ]) is a locality on the Swedish island of Gotland. Väskinde is also the name of the larger populated area, socken (not to be confused with parish). It comprises the same area as the administrative Väskinde District, established on 1 January 2016.","wpu":"Väskinde","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/V%C3%A4skinde_kyrka.JPG/960px-V%C3%A4skinde_kyrka.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Hejdeby Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":57.6304,"lo":18.4427,"d":9447,"ds":"Hejdeby Church (Swedish: Hejdeby kyrka) is a medieval church in Hejdeby on the Swedish island of Gotland. The church was built in stages during the 13th century, and contains medieval murals from two different periods. Hejdeby Church is part of the Diocese of Visby within the Church of Sweden.","wpu":"Hejdeby Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Hejdeby-kyrka-Gotland-torn1.jpg/960px-Hejdeby-kyrka-Gotland-torn1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Väskinde Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":57.690556,"lo":18.422778,"d":9937,"ds":"Väskinde Church (Swedish: Väskinde kyrka) is a medieval Lutheran church in Väskinde on the island of Gotland, Sweden. It belongs to the Diocese of Visby.","wpu":"Väskinde Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Igrexa_de_V%C3%A4skinde_2.jpg/960px-Igrexa_de_V%C3%A4skinde_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Visby (Swedish: [ˈvǐːsbʏ] ) is an urban area in Sweden and the seat of Gotland Municipality in Gotland County on the island of Gotland with 24,330 inhabitants as of 2017. Visby is also the episcopal see for the Diocese of Visby. The Hanseatic city of Visby is one of the best-preserved medieval cities in Scandinavia, and, since 1995, it has been on the UNESCO World Heritage Site list.","wpu":"Visby","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/0522Visby_domkyrka.jpg/960px-0522Visby_domkyrka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}